# Swift Standards

## Naming Conventions

```swift
// ✅ Classes and Structs - PascalCase
class WindowManager { }
struct CacheEntry { }

// ✅ Methods and Variables - camelCase
func refreshWindows() { }
var selectedWindowIndex: Int

// ✅ Constants - camelCase (not SCREAMING_SNAKE)
static let cacheExpiration = 1.0
static let perfLogFile = "/tmp/alttab_perf.log"

// ✅ Boolean predicates - start with is/has/should/needs
var isFirstSummon: Bool
var shouldShowTheUser: Bool
var needsVisibilityUpdate: Bool
```

## Static vs Instance

```swift
// ✅ Stateless utilities - static methods
class Windows {
    static func refreshWhichWindowsToShowTheUser() { }
    static var list = [Window]()
}

// ✅ Stateful objects - instance methods
class Window {
    func updateVisibility() { }
    var shouldShowTheUser: Bool
}
```

## Conditional Compilation

```swift
// ✅ GOOD - DEBUG-only code
#if DEBUG
static let perfLogFile = "/tmp/alttab_perf.log"
#endif

// ✅ GOOD - Entire method eliminated in Release
@inline(__always)
static func perf(_ message: @autoclosure () -> String) {
    #if DEBUG
    // Implementation
    #endif
}
```

## Optional Handling

```swift
// ✅ GOOD - Guard for early exit
guard let window = windows.first else { return }

// ✅ GOOD - Optional chaining
let focusedId = application.focusedWindow?.cgWindowId

// ✅ GOOD - Nil coalescing with context
let pid = frontmostPid ?? -1
Logger.perf("Frontmost PID: \(pid)")
```

## Type Safety

```swift
// ✅ GOOD - Explicit types for clarity
let shortcutIndex: Int = 0
let windows: [Window] = []

// ✅ GOOD - Type inference when obvious
let cache = [Int32: CGWindowID?]()
```

## Code Organization

1. **Static properties** → **Static methods** → **Instance properties** → **Instance methods**
2. **Group related functionality** with `// MARK: - Section Name`
3. **Keep methods focused** - one responsibility per method
4. **Extract complex logic** into helper methods
